hadiths[9]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2116","Ibn 'Umar narrated that the Messenger of Allah (S.A.W) said:\It is not right for a Muslim man to spend two nights"""
"2117","Abu Hurairah narrated that the Messenger of Allah (S.A.W) said:\Indeed a man"""
"2118","Talhah bin Musarrif said:\I said to Ibn Abi Awfi: Did the Messenger of Allah (S.A.W) leave a will?' He said: 'No' I said: 'How is the will written"""
"2119","He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to perform cupping (*hijamah*) on the two jugular veins (*al-akhda'ayn*) and the upper back (*al-kahil*). He ﷺ would perform cupping on the seventeenth, the nineteenth, and the twenty-first (of the lunar month).\n\n**Abu 'Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said:** There are narrations on this topic from Ibn 'Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) and Ma'qil ibn Yasar (may Allah be pleased with him). And this is a **Hasan Sahih** hadith."

"\n- """
"2120","Amr bin Kharajah narrated:\The Prophet (s.a.w) gave a Khutbah upon his she-camel"""
"2121","Al-Harith narrated from 'Ali:\The Prophet (s.a.w) judged with the debt before the will"""
"2122","Abu Habibah At-Ta'i said:\My brother willed a portion of his wealth to me. So I met Abu Ad-Darda and said: 'My brother has willed a portion of his wealth to me"""
"2123","Urwah narrated that :'Aishah had informed him that Barrirah came to her ('Aishah) seeking her help for her writ of emancipation"
"2124","Aishah narrated that she wanted to buy Barrirah but (her owners) stipulated that they should have her Wala'"
